{
  "requirement": "`habeas author <full-name> [--config <name>] [--missing | --force] [--stdout] [-v|--verbose]`\nMUST author the evidence of one existing requirement or named example in the\ncurrent project, under {cite}`requirements.authoring.refresh`. It MUST report the\nselected subject, backend, model, evidence destination, and usage-record path on\ncompletion. The evidence destination MUST identify the evidence-file path by\ndefault or stdout when `--stdout` is selected. In stdout mode, the completion\nreport and diagnostics MUST go to stderr. `author-evidence` MUST remain an alias\nfor the single-subject command.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Determination: false.** The single-subject command does not implement the `[--missing | --force]` part of the stated invocation, and no `{fixme}` acknowledges the gap.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. `habeas author <full-name> [--config <name>] [--missing | --force] [--stdout] [-v|--verbose]` MUST author one existing requirement or example, \"under `requirements.authoring.refresh`\".\n2. It MUST report the selected subject, backend, model, evidence destination and usage-record path on completion.\n3. The evidence destination MUST be the evidence-file path by default, or `stdout` with `--stdout`.\n4. In stdout mode, the completion report and diagnostics MUST go to stderr.\n5. `author-evidence` MUST remain an alias.\n\n**Met and tested**\n- **Subject authoring (1):** `Command::Author` and `main` in `src/main.rs` call `author_evidence_with_options`, which goes through `configured_assessment`. `AuthoringSubject::parse` and `AuthoringSubject::sources` resolve the subject, and `AssessmentSources::prepare` in `src/authoring/inputs.rs` rejects an unknown name with \"no matching requirement or named example\". `author_rejects_unknown_subjects_and_conflicting_targets` tests the unknown-name failure.\n- **Completion report (2):** `main` prints `subject: backend / model`, `Evidence: <path>` and `Usage: <path>`. `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` checks the model, `Evidence:` and `Usage:`.\n- **Evidence destination (3):** `EvidenceOutput` and `configured_assessment` write the file or stdout, and the report shows the path or \"Evidence: stdout\". `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` asserts `Evidence: stdout\\n`.\n- **Stderr in stdout mode (4):** `main` uses `eprintln!` for the report and the false-judgment notice when there is no evidence path. The same test asserts stdout holds only the JSON and stderr holds the report.\n- **Alias (5):** `#[command(alias = \"author-evidence\")]` is on `Command::Author`. The tests invoke `author-evidence`.\n- **Other flags:** `--config`, `--stdout` and `-v`/`--verbose` are handled in `main` and `configured_assessment`. The tests in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` cover them: `authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file`, `verbose_single_author_reports_only_false_rationale_without_source_inputs`, and the stdout test.\n\n**Gap: `--missing` / `--force`**\n- The stated syntax includes `[--missing | --force]`, and the requirement applies `requirements.authoring.refresh` to the command.\n- `refresh` says every `habeas author` form MUST accept `--missing` and `--force`. They are mutually exclusive and `--missing` is the default. `--stdout` implies `--force`. The command reports the number of subjects skipped as current. It preserves current records without invoking a model, and succeeds without resolving model configuration when no assessment is needed.\n- The `Author` variant in `src/main.rs` declares only `subject`, `all`, `config`, `stdout`, `verbose` and `confirm`. A ripgrep of `src/main.rs` for `force|missing` returned nothing. A repo-wide search found no `--missing` or `--force` argument, and no single-subject skip-as-current logic.\n- `author_evidence_with_options` and `configured_assessment` always assess the named subject. They never check whether existing evidence is current, never report a skipped-current count, and never take a force/missing mode.\n- Because `--missing` is meant to be the default, `habeas author <name>` on a current record should skip it. The code reassesses it instead. `habeas author --force <name>` or `--missing <name>` would be rejected by clap.\n- Only the `--all` path (`select_subjects` in `src/authoring/batch.rs`) skips current records. That serves `requirements.authoring.batch`, not the single-subject invocation.\n- Nothing carries an `{impl}` for `requirements.authoring.refresh` (the references tool shows only `{cite}` sites), and no test exercises `--missing` or `--force`.\n- The code that decides to apply the cited `refresh` requirement in the single-subject case is therefore missing, and untested. No `{fixme}` reference acknowledges this gap, so it is unacknowledged.\n\nThe assessment therefore fails on the unimplemented `[--missing | --force]` option of the invocation.",
  "references": "aa874c5d7e7b17bf9c286d0581cdede3b7369585ff60617270a28e1bb4d4ddab",
